      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That is twice the usual maximum daily dose of 2,550 mg for immediate-release metformin, or 2,000 mg for extended-release in many labels. A single 1,700 mg dose is also well above the usual maximum of 1,000 mg per dose. At this level there is a high risk of GI toxicity and lactic acidosis.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals** (2,550 mg/day, the maximum)\n- **1,700 mg/day divided**, for example 850 mg twice daily\n- Another dose, such as 500 mg or 1,000 mg\n\nTell me the dose you want and I'll enter it right away. If 1,700 mg three times daily is what you intended, please confirm that. I'd suggest checking it with pharmacy first, and I can add a note to the order."
      }
